    <task workspace="0.5in">
      <introduction>
        <p>
          Determine whether each story would require a linear or non-linear model. Explain your choice.
        </p>
      </introduction>

      <sidebyside>
          <p>
            Geppetto carved Pinocchio a 2-inch long nose. Each time Pinocchio tells a lie, his nose grows 3 inches. 
          </p>
       
          <p>
            Geppetto carved Pinocchio a 2-inch long nose. Each time Pinocchio tells a lie, his nose doubles in length. 
          </p>
          
       
          <p>
            Geppetto carved Pinocchio a 2-inch long nose. Each time Pinocchio tells a lie, his nose grows from its previous length by the same number of inches as the number of lies he has told. For example, after 1 lie, his nose will be 2 + 1 = 3 inches long. After 2 lies, his nose will be 3 + 2 = 5 inches long. 
          </p>
          
        </sidebyside>
    </task>
    <task workspace="0.5in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            How can you tell a story can be modeled by a linear equation?
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

    <task workspace="0.5in">
      <introduction>
        <p>
          Categorize each equation as linear or non-linear. Explain your choice.
        </p>
      </introduction>

      <sidebyside>
        
          <p>
            <m>y = 3x + 4</m>
          </p>
         
          <p>
            <m>y = 2^x + 3</m>
          </p>
          
          <p>
            <m>y = x^2 + 1</m>
          </p>
          </sidebyside>
      </task>
   

   <task workspace="0.5in">
        <statement>
          <p>
            What does an equation of a linear equation look like?
          </p>
        </statement>
      </task>

